  "published": "2026-09-16T18:45:37.767Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Faster and leaner reading and writing with unchanged output: writers format each record into one reusable buffer (half to two thirds less allocation, 12-20% faster) and readers scan their input as a span instead of one character at a time (a third to two fifths faster). FixedLengthOptions.IsLongRecordRejected, off by default, refuses a fixed-length record longer than the schema with the same exception a short record gets. The eleven numeric columns derive from a public NumberColumn base, so a column for another numeric type is a constructor away. Fixed: unsubscribing from IReader.RecordParsed never took effect. New Format overloads on IColumnDefinition and ColumnDefinition write into a buffer, with a default that falls back to the string form so existing custom columns keep working. EnumColumn.Parser and Formatter are declared non-nullable. Source-compatible with 7.0.0; recompile.",
